## Your flow is ready: `SlackChannelDescription`

**File:** `SlackChannelDescription/SlackChannelDescription/SlackChannelDescription.flow`

### What it does

| Step | Node | What happens |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Manual Trigger** | You kick it off on demand — no schedule needed |
| 2 | **Get Channel Info** | Calls the Slack connector using the channel name/ID you provide |
| 3 | **End** | Returns the channel's description (purpose text) back to you |

### How to run it

When you trigger the flow, pass one input:
- **`channelName`** — the Slack channel name (e.g. `general`) or its ID (e.g. `C0123ABCDEF`)

The flow returns one output:
- **`channelDescription`** — the description text set on that channel

